<%# Profile photo row.

    Locals: user (required).

    Posts to its OWN route (profile_avatar_path), not the shared PATCH /profile.
    An attachment param submitted empty PURGES the attachment, so a combined form
    would delete the picture every time someone edited their name. Keeping the
    file field in a form of its own makes that trap unreachable rather than
    merely avoided.

    A plain file field for now. The engine already ships a crop modal
    (studio/modals/_crop_photo plus the cropPhotoModal factory), but wiring it
    needs a modal host and the cropper assets on the page; this row is designed to
    be swapped to it without changing the endpoint.
%>
<div class="flex items-center gap-5">
  <%= render "components/avatar", user: user, size: "lg" %>

  <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
    <%= form_with url: profile_avatar_path, method: :patch, scope: :profile, multipart: true,
                  data: { turbo: false }, class: "flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3" do |form| %>
      <%= form.file_field :avatar,
                          accept: Studio::ProfileImage::ALLOWED_CONTENT_TYPES.join(","),
                          class: "text-sm text-secondary file:mr-3 file:py-1.5 file:px-3 file:rounded file:border-0 file:text-sm file:font-semibold file:bg-surface-alt file:text-heading" %>
      <%= form.submit "Save photo", class: "btn btn-primary btn-sm" %>
    <% end %>
    <p class="text-muted text-xs mt-2"><%= Studio::ProfileImage::MESSAGE %></p>
  </div>
</div>
